TITLE:: MS20OTA
summary:: Later MS-20 filter revision (KLM-307) with dual OTA stages and resonance feedback limiter
categories:: UGens>Filters>Nonlinear
related:: Classes/MS20Diode, Classes/MS20TPT, Classes/MS20SK

DESCRIPTION::
MS20OTA models the later revision of the Korg MS-20 filter, constructed around the KLM-307 daughterboard using dual Operational Transconductance Amplifiers (LM13600 OTAs).

Historically and architecturally, MS20OTA is fundamentally distinct from the early Korg-35 filter:
LIST::
## Buffering: The two OTA integrator stages are uncoupled by an intermediate unity-gain buffer. Unlike the early Korg-35 Sallen-Key circuit, there is strong isolation and NO inter-stage loading between the two stages.
## Critical Gain: Because there is no inter-stage loading, the linear damping factor is (2 - K) rather than (3 - K), causing the onset of self-oscillation to occur at K = 2.0 rather than K = 3.0.
## Diode Location: The back-to-back clipping diodes are placed in the resonance feedback amplifier, rather than in the forward amplifier path.
## Timbre: Because the forward OTA stages remain linear, passband signals do not distort. The clipping diodes selectively saturate and compress only the resonant peak frequencies that circulate through the feedback loop. This produces a smoother, more liquid, "singing" resonance characteristic.
## Modes: Implements both Low-Pass (mode 0, 12 dB/octave roll-off) and authentic historical MS-20 High-Pass (mode 1, 6 dB/octave low-frequency roll-off with 2nd-order resonance peak).
::

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: ar
Create an audio-rate MS20OTA filter instance.

ARGUMENT:: in
Audio rate input signal.

ARGUMENT:: freq
Cutoff frequency in Hz (internally clamped to [10 Hz, 0.49 * sampleRate]). Supports scalar, control-rate (kr), and audio-rate (ar) modulation for sample-accurate filter FM.

ARGUMENT:: res
Normalized resonance control in [0.0, 1.0]. Mapped to feedback gain teletype::K = res * 2.5::. Self-oscillation begins at teletype::res = 0.8:: (K = 2.0).

ARGUMENT:: drive
Dimensionless feedback drive scaling (nominal = 1.0, range 0.01 .. 10.0). Higher values compress the resonant peak more heavily.

ARGUMENT:: mode
Filter mode selection (evaluated at synth instantiation / i-rate):
LIST::
## 0 = Low-pass filter (12 dB/octave roll-off, clean passband, feedback diode resonance saturation)
## 1 = Authentic MS-20 High-pass filter (6 dB/octave low-frequency roll-off, feedback diode resonance saturation)
::

ARGUMENT:: oversample
Oversampling selection (evaluated at synth instantiation / i-rate):
LIST::
## 0 = 1x base sample rate (standard, ultra-low CPU, minimal latency).
## 1 = 2x internal polyphase halfband oversampling (> 70 dB stopband rejection, < 0.0005 dB passband ripple). Drastically eliminates foldover aliasing during extreme overdrive (drive > 4.0) or high-frequency audio-rate filter FM.
::

returns:: An audio-rate UGen output.

EXAMPLES::

code::
s.boot;

// 1. Low-Pass sweep with singing, liquid OTA resonance
(
x = {
    var src = Saw.ar([110, 110.5]) * 0.15;
    var cutoff = SinOsc.kr(0.15).exprange(150, 6000);
    // Notice how the passband stays clean while the resonant peak sings
    var sig = MS20OTA.ar(src, freq: cutoff, res: 0.75, drive: 1.0, mode: 0);
    sig * 0.25
}.play;
)
x.free;

// 2. Pure Autonomous Self-Oscillation (singing sine tone at cutoff)
(
x = {
    var trigger = Impulse.ar(0) * 0.01;
    var pitch = MouseX.kr(55, 880, \exponential);
    var sig = MS20OTA.ar(trigger, freq: pitch, res: 0.95, drive: 1.0, mode: 0);
    (sig * 0.3) ! 2
}.play;
)
x.free;

// 3. Driven High-Pass sweep on drum loop / noise
(
x = {
    var src = PinkNoise.ar(0.2) + Pulse.ar(55, 0.4, 0.1);
    var cutoff = XLine.kr(40, 4000, 10);
    var sig = MS20OTA.ar(src, freq: cutoff, res: 0.7, drive: 2.0, mode: 1);
    (sig * 0.25) ! 2
}.play;
)
x.free;
::
